{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom at a668051e39ce7060ef96cfb02d83b2a20c701b0d on request/commitment-honesty.\n\nThe commitment projection stopped saying two things the log does not support.\n\nAn acknowledged completion could be erased. Retirement was read before reports, so retiring a request whose report had already been ratified overwrote satisfied with cancelled: the work was done, the requester said so, and the board then reported it as called off. Measured against this workroom's own log, five commitments sit in exactly that state. Satisfaction is now settled first and is terminal, and the row keeps its stale qualifier because the world did move under it. Retiring the request afterwards says the request is no longer live, not that the work never happened.\n\nThe fold admits a supersession from the target's own author or from any ratifier, but the projection labelled every retired promise reneged and every retired request cancelled without asking who acted, so an authority withdrawing someone's promise charged that person with walking away from it. Retirement now carries the actors holding it, and a third-party withdrawal reads revoked, which names nobody as having failed. That word reaches the query filter, the terminal lane, the MCP enum and its reference page, and the browser's closed statuses, colour and label, so it cannot arrive somewhere with no word for it. The docset gate and a lane-table test each caught one of those omissions.\n\nAll six terminal states now have tests; none had one before. Both fixes are mutation-checked: ignoring the superseding actor reproduces the blame misattribution on three rows, and restoring the old ordering reproduces the erased satisfaction.\n\nThe pinned legacy projection changes by three lines — the row gains its report, reads satisfied, and keeps stale — which is the migration that guard exists to force into the open rather than let pass unnoticed.\n\ngo vet, the full Go suite, tsc and the browser tests all pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/commitment-honesty","commit":"a668051e39ce7060ef96cfb02d83b2a20c701b0d","head":"a668051e39ce7060ef96cfb02d83b2a20c701b0d","path":"internal/workroom"}}